WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.037
Here's what a failing run looks like,
so the first one isn't a surprise.

2
00:00:04.037 --> 00:00:07.162
These rows come from the
kit's own fictional tenant.

3
00:00:07.162 --> 00:00:10.766
One user group shrank by a
quarter since the last snapshot,

4
00:00:10.766 --> 00:00:14.670
and a device group doubled, so both
are findings; in a mover proof,

5
00:00:14.670 --> 00:00:18.049
a finding on a group the move
shouldn't touch means stop.

6
00:00:18.049 --> 00:00:19.625
Read the status carefully.

7
00:00:19.625 --> 00:00:21.475
Fail means at least one finding.

8
00:00:21.475 --> 00:00:23.150
Warn means something to review.

9
00:00:23.150 --> 00:00:28.050
Not applicable means nothing to check or
a missing input, and it's never a pass.

10
00:00:28.050 --> 00:00:31.175
Error means a read
failed, also never a pass.

11
00:00:31.175 --> 00:00:34.963
On the right is the evidence to
keep, joined on the person key.

12
00:00:34.963 --> 00:00:39.025
Entra ID keeps most of it for thirty
days at best, and the provenance

13
00:00:39.025 --> 00:00:43.150
record not at all, so route everything
out from the pilot's first day.
